brexit now that the UK has officially  notified the European Council of its  intention to leave what's next the next  steps were agreed by all Member States  years ago and are set out in article 50  of the EU treaty the other 27 leaders of  the European Council adopted guidelines  for the negotiations with the UK those  guidelines can be amended throughout for  negotiations the ministers in the  Council of the EU also meeting in an EU  27 format authorized the opening of  negotiations they appoint the Commission  as the EU negotiator and adopt  negotiating directives on behalf of the  eu-27 the Commission negotiates with the  UK reporting back to the leaders in the  European Council and the ministers in  the council the European Parliament is  closely and regularly informed for as  long as the UK remains a member of the  EU it participates in all European  Council and council meetings except when  breaks it is discussed after the end of  negotiations the consent of the European  Parliament is required the deal is then  ready to be concluded by the council  when the agreement enters into force the  UK is no longer an EU member and the EU  treaties ceased to apply to it find out  more on the council website  you
 

